{"content":[{"c":["ANAK, ANAKIM*, ANAKITES"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Ancestor of a race of giants in old Canaan. When Israel first reached Canaan, the Anakim were well established in Hebron. Ten of the 12 spies Moses sent into Canaan (",{"href":"?bref=Num.13.17-22","r":"Num.13.17-22","rawR":"Num.13.17-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.13.17-22","value":"Num.13.17-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 13:17-22"},") were terrified by the size of the Anakim (",{"href":"?bref=Num.13.31","r":"Num.13.31","rawR":"Num.13.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.13.31","value":"Num.13.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 13:31"},"). Their terror led to a rebellion at Kadesh-barnea (",{"href":"?bref=Num.14.39-45","r":"Num.14.39-45","rawR":"Num.14.39-45","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.14.39-45","value":"Num.14.39-45"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 14:39-45"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.1.19-46","r":"Deut.1.19-46","rawR":"Deut.1.19-46","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.1.19-46","value":"Deut.1.19-46"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 1:19-46"},") and another 38 years of wandering. When the Israelites were finally ready to enter Canaan, God promised his help against the famed Anak giants (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.9.1-3","r":"Deut.9.1-3","rawR":"Deut.9.1-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.9.1-3","value":"Deut.9.1-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 9:1-3"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["The two spies who were not afraid of the Anakim were both involved in their defeat. Joshua defeated the Anakim living in Hebron, Debir, Anab, and all the region of Judah (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.11.21-23","r":"Josh.11.21-23","rawR":"Josh.11.21-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.11.21-23","value":"Josh.11.21-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 11:21-23"},"). Those who survived were left only in the Philistine cities of Gaza, Gath, and Ashdod. The other spy, Caleb, was responsible for the defeat of the Anakim chiefs Sheshai, Ahiman, and Talmai at Hebron; Caleb’s nephew Othniel was the hero of Debir (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.14-17","r":"Josh.15.14-17","rawR":"Josh.15.14-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.14-17","value":"Josh.15.14-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 15:14-17"},"). Hebron had earlier been called Kiriath-arba for Anak’s father Arba, a great hero of the Anakim (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.14.15","r":"Josh.14.15","rawR":"Josh.14.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.14.15","value":"Josh.14.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 14:15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.21.11","r":"Josh.21.11","rawR":"Josh.21.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.21.11","value":"Josh.21.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:11"},"). The fact that the Anakim survived in the Philistine cities of Gaza, Gath, and Ashdod leads to the supposition that Goliath of Gath may have been a descendant of these giants (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.17.4-7","r":"1Sam.17.4-7","rawR":"1Sam.17.4-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.17.4-7","value":"1Sam.17.4-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 17:4-7"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Giants_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Giants_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Giants_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Giants"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"AnakAnakimAnakites","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 13:17-22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.13.17-22","rawQueryValue":"Num.13.17-22","sourceRefExact":"Num.13.17-22"},{"anchorText":"Nm 13:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.13.31","rawQueryValue":"Num.13.31","sourceRefExact":"Num.13.31"},{"anchorText":"Nm 14:39-45","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.14.39-45","rawQueryValue":"Num.14.39-45","sourceRefExact":"Num.14.39-45"},{"anchorText":"Dt 1:19-46","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.1.19-46","rawQueryValue":"Deut.1.19-46","sourceRefExact":"Deut.1.19-46"},{"anchorText":"Dt 9:1-3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.9.1-3","rawQueryValue":"Deut.9.1-3","sourceRefExact":"Deut.9.1-3"},{"anchorText":"Jos 11:21-23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.11.21-23","rawQueryValue":"Josh.11.21-23","sourceRefExact":"Josh.11.21-23"},{"anchorText":"Jos 15:14-17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.14-17","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.14-17","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.14-17"},{"anchorText":"Jos 14:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.14.15","rawQueryValue":"Josh.14.15","sourceRefExact":"Josh.14.15"},{"anchorText":"21:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.21.11","rawQueryValue":"Josh.21.11","sourceRefExact":"Josh.21.11"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 17:4-7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.17.4-7","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.17.4-7","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.17.4-7"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"246265702cabb28b2e132d80f11f246bd602bd11393b52ff19e5676c6bdaab55","sourceItemName":"AnakAnakimAnakites","sourceItemOrder":328,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"AnakAnakimAnakites","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Anak, Anakim*, Anakites","title":"Anak, Anakim*, Anakites","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}